# ExamFlow — Conflict-Free Exam Seating & Invigilation System

A full-stack Java system that auto-generates exam seating plans, ensures no two students from the same class sit adjacent, assigns invigilators, and lets students find their seat in real time.

🚀 Live Demo • Backend Code • Frontend Code

## 🌟 What is ExamFlow?

ExamFlow is a full-stack system I built to replace the manual, spreadsheet-driven way colleges handle exam seating. Instead of a staff member manually checking that no two students from the same class sit together, the system does it automatically using a constraint-satisfaction algorithm — and goes further by handling invigilator assignment, live absentee tracking, and instant seat lookup for students.

It doesn't just place students in seats. It explains why seating fails when it can't fit everyone, broadcasts live updates the moment something changes, and gives students a self-serve way to find their seat without asking staff.

## ✨ Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| 🪑 Auto Seating | Generates a full seating plan enforcing "no same class adjacent" |
| 🧑‍🏫 Invigilator Assignment | Round-robin assigns invigilators across all halls |
| 🔍 Student Seat Lookup | Enter roll number → get hall, row, column + QR code |
| 🔔 Live Absentee Alerts | Mark a student absent → seat frees instantly, live WebSocket alert to all admins |
| 📋 Conflict Explanation | If seating fails, explains exactly why (class, count, capacity) |
| 🔐 Admin Access Control | Password-gated admin panel, public student lookup |

